; The one variable: `outline_render_priority` against the fill's `render_priority` of 0. Left: -1,
; the default, so the outline draws first and the fill covers its inside. Right: 0, where Godot
; keeps the draws of one instance newest first (render_forward_clustered.cpp:4147-4148), so the
; outline, surface 0, draws after the fill and covers its edges. Two labels with one fat yellow
; fill mean the order of the surfaces at one priority is lost.
